# ── ROM content: never committed, in any form (CLAUDE.md §2 rule 7) ──────────
# Reference sets live OUTSIDE the tree in $ROMDIR; these patterns are defense
# in depth in case anything ROM-shaped ever lands inside the repo.
*.zip
*.7z
*.bin
*.rom
*.key
# CPS-2 part-number naming (vsav/vsav2/vhunt2 program, gfx, qsound files)
vm3*.*
vs2*.*
vh2*.*
*.03[a-e]
*.04[a-e]
*.[0-9][0-9]m
dl-1425*
# Decrypted / intermediate ROM images
build/out/
build/cache/
*.decrypted
*.prg

# ── Emulator working dirs and artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
# emu/fbneo is a git submodule (gitlink only; its content is never committed here)
emu/*/build/
cfg/
nvram/
diff/
inp/
snap/
sta/
mame.ini
ui.ini
plugin.ini

# ── Tooling noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
re/ghidra/*
!re/ghidra/.keep
!re/ghidra/README.md

# ── OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*

# ── Exceptions: savestates/replays that tests depend on are force-added ──────
# (git add -f, per CLAUDE.md savestate hygiene; no blanket un-ignore here)
build/donovan/
# GATE-WRITTEN BUILD DIRS (14z-95, GitHub #97). These two are the ONLY build
# dirs a test writes to on every run — run_battery_m2.sh builds into
# build/donovan6, and test_m2a_stage4_code.sh used to build into
# build/donovan_stage4_gate. They carried 19 TRACKED generator outputs
# committed at 14z-47/48/49, so running the suite rewrote committed files and
# `git status` after a test run showed a diff. A pre-commit chain whose own
# side effect is a diff is one people learn to scroll past, and that is how a
# REAL unexpected modification gets missed.
#
# THE RULE, and it is narrower than "build outputs should not be tracked":
# a directory a GATE WRITES TO cannot also be a TRACKED REFERENCE. The other
# ~200 tracked build dirs (hui*, pyron*, m3b_merged*, scratch/*) are frozen
# historical builds that nothing overwrites, so they are untouched by this —
# whether THEY should be tracked is a separate, repo-wide question.
#
# Nothing required the tracked copies: only tools/overlay_port.py names one
# (build/donovan6/select_tiles.json, an optional `if exists` read), and that
# tool has NO caller. The build's rompath — which ~10 gates DO read — was
# never tracked and is regenerated by the battery as before.
build/donovan6/
build/donovan_stage4_gate/

# EMULATOR STATE AND SCRATCH (14z-95, maintainer-ruled 2026-08-18 after the
# tracked-build-dir measurement: 2,754 files / 304 MB, 225 of 284 top-level
# entries referenced by nothing).
#
# (1) Emulator state — MAME nvram, config and debugger scripts. Machine-local
#     and GENERATED: run_replay_guarded.sh writes guard_go.dbs itself
#     (`printf 'go\n' > "$WORK/guard_go.dbs"`), so the committed copies were
#     stale artifacts of old runs with no evidentiary value.
# (2) build/scratch/** — scratch by name. Its FOUR real tools were moved to
#     tools/ first (audit_venue_consumers, audit_palette_ptr_rows,
#     audit_palette_block_width, audit_slot0f_assumptions); two of them are
#     documented as runnable commands in docs/game/atlas/venue_assets.md, so
#     untracking scratch blindly would have deleted documented tooling.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: the per-build patch.json/placements.json/
# regions.json of the other ~200 dirs. For SUPERSEDED builds whose manifests
# have moved on, that metadata is the only record of what the build WAS —
# HANDOFF calls the freeze tags "the only way back" while also noting nobody
# has re-verified the older ones, so rebuild-from-tag is UNTESTED and this is
# the hedge. Maintainer ruled: keep them.
build/**/*.nv
build/**/*.ini
build/**/*.dbs
build/**/*.cfg
build/scratch/

# Generated CPS-2 WIDE romset overlays: directories of ABSOLUTE symlinks into
# $ROMDIR plus one clone zip, rebuilt in one command (HANDOFF). Tracking them
# put a stale absolute symlink in git, which dangled the moment the repo path
# changed and produced a false gate FAIL (14z-61, docs/GOTCHAS.md).
build/wide0/rompath/
build/wide_canary/rompath/
build/manifest/probe_*.toml
build/probe_*/
build/probe_*.log

# ── 14z-91 (GitHub #39/#40, maintainer-ruled) ────────────────────────────
# WIDE extension program members. `vsw.*`, NOT `vsw*.*`: the pattern must
# not also swallow authored sources that happen to start with those letters.
# Measured today these are 0xFF fill (12 of 16 a single repeated byte), so
# the audit's "8 MiB of ROM-derived output" was false — but the profile
# targets ~338 KB of PORTED PROGRAM ROM landing in exactly these members,
# and rule 7 is about what the repo will hold tomorrow, not today.
vsw.*

# Root-anchored build/clone trees that were never meant to be committed.
# The worktrees entry is not cosmetic: 471 MB of duplicated tools/tests/docs
# under .claude/worktrees/ makes every retraction-discipline grep return
# pre-move copies, so a session can "fix" a claim in a worktree and believe
# it done (paid for repeatedly in 14z-90 and again in 14z-91 — every grep in
# this repo now needs `| grep -v worktrees`). Scoped to .claude/worktrees/,
# NOT a blanket .claude/, so agent/skill config stays trackable.
/fbneo/
/mame/
/.claude/worktrees/

# Harness output dropped at the repo root when CHECKSUM_OUT is unset
# (tests/lua/replay.lua:50, replay_guard.lua:51 default to this name). It is
# a run artifact, not source — untracked and unignored it sat as permanent
# `??` noise, which is the same disease as GitHub #97: a test run should not
# leave the tree looking dirty, or people learn to scroll past git status.
replay_checksums.txt

# GENERATED, NEVER COMMITTED (14z-107 (10)). docs/project/mister_core.md
# carries the ASCII figures; the rich page is emitted by the committed
# generator tools/mk_mister_page.py, because a hand-copied artifact goes
# stale silently and this one draws a memory map whose slack is 0.2%.
docs/project/mister_core.html
